    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d767">

                <pb facs="0785" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4068: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-12T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1919,
                                8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:56 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1136. Referring to telegram to Department from Legation Copenhagen number
                        3721,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d767-f1"/> following message is being despatched
                    by cable to Legation, <pb facs="0786" n="674" xml:id="pg674"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Your 241, March 8, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="9"
                                xml:id="d767-f2"/> A mission including necessary experts will leave
                            here about week for Copenhagen, Stockholm, Helsingfors, Reval to
                            investigate economic military situation and the question of credits.
                            Please prepare useful data, concise form, to hand them on arrival. Chief
                            of this mission is Lieutenant Colonel
                                [Warwick] Greene personally known to you.[”]</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
